  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Circular denim capacity building, Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project builds upon the feasibility study (PST20PK01) in Pakistan, 2020-2021. This pilot study has revealed that white recycled cotton, sourced from the hotel industry in the Netherlands, can effectively be utilized in producing jeans in Pakistan.The current project aims to scale up these results amongst a larger group of companies in the denim supply chain in Pakistan.The project aims to establish one pool of fifteen to twenty qualified Pakistani companies in the denim textile chain from around Lahore in which the manufacturers can produce products from post-consumer waste (PCW) for the denim supply chain that satisfies customer requirements and provides transparency over material input and processes. Individual training by experts, workshops, and coaching helps this project succeed.</narrative>
  </description>
